# Thranduil's Company: the extra land play needs "another Elf" that Bot1 controls. Bot2 controls a Llanowar Elves, which does not count,
# and the Company is not another Elf than itself: on turn 3 Bot1 plays its one land, a Swamp (landfall puts two counters on the
# Company, the only creature it may target - Bot2's Elves is not legal), and may not play a second land, a Plains (refused).

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Black Lotus
Mox Sapphire
Thranduil's Company
Swamp
Plains
Island
Island x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Llanowar Elves
Island x18

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Green)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Thranduil's Company.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
! Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play

[Expect]
Bot1.LandsPlayed = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Thranduil's Company.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = 2
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Colors.Count = 0
